      "abstract": "Abstract The expression \u201chistorical materialism\u201d was first used by G. V. Plekhanov, the \u201cfather\u201d of Russian Marxism, to indicate the social theory of Marxism. Marx and Engels, however, always referred to their doctrine as a \u201cmaterialist conception of history\u201d and never used the phrase \u201chistorical materialism.\u201d The foundation of the materialist theory of history was first formulated extensively in the manuscripts of 1845, later published under the name The German Ideology , a work in which the influence of the Scottish Enlightenment was clearly discernible, as Marx and Engels stressed the importance of the division of labor and forms of property as the moving forces behind the development of societies. On the other hand, Marx and Engels criticized Enlightenment social philosophies for their mechanical cause\u2013effect explanations and proposed instead a dialectical view of the development of human society.",
